格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"一个自主的高级智能伙伴，不仅分析问题，更持续工作直到完成实现和验证。","id":"gh:1064776002","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"helloagents","slug":"hellowind777/helloagents","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"一个自主的高级智能伙伴，不仅分析问题，更持续工作直到完成实现和验证。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# HelloAGENTS"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**A workflow layer for AI coding CLIs: skills, project knowledge, delivery checks, safer config writ"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"es, and resumable execution.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Looking for `v2.x`? The old Python line now lives in helloagents-archive. The `v3` "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"line is a full rewrite based on Node.js, Markdown rules, skills, and small runtime scripts."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> 🏅 This project is linked & recognized by the LINUX DO community."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- What HelloAGENTS Does\n- Core Features\n- Quick Start\n- CLI Management\n- Commands in Chat\n- Project "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"Knowledge Base\n- Workflow and Delivery\n- Configuration\n- How Each CLI Is Integrated\n- Verification\n-"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" FAQ\n- Troubleshooting\n- License"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## What HelloAGENTS Does"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"AI coding CLIs can move fast, but they can also stop at advice, skip checks, lose project context, s"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"hift responsibility when tasks get hard, or report completion before the work is really done."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"HelloAGENTS adds a workflow layer on top of Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Grok Build, Cursor, and Codex C"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"LI. It anchors the agent as a capable executor, blocks responsibility-shifting patterns, helps the a"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"gent choose the right path, use task-specific quality skills, keep a project knowledge base, and ver"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"ify work before delivery."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**Without HelloAGENTS**"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**With HelloAGENTS**"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Problem | Without HelloAGENTS | With HelloAGENTS |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Stops too early | Ends with suggestions | Continues into build, verify, and closeout |\n| Shifts re"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"sponsibility | Refuses hard tasks, suggests other tools | Exhausts alternative paths, stays on task "},{"id":"p14s3","text":"|\n| Quality is inconsistent | Depends on each prompt | 14 quality skills activate by task type |\n| C"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"ontext is scattered | Plans live in chat history | Project knowledge and plan files stay on disk |\n|"},{"id":"p14s5","text":" Completion is vague | Natural language says “done” | Delivery checks use state, evidence, and verif"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"ication |\n| Config writes are risky | CLI files can drift | Install, update, cleanup, and doctor flo"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"ws check managed files |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Core Features"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### 1) 14 built-in workflow skills"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"HelloAGENTS ships 14 built-in skills. They are loaded only when the current stage needs them, so sim"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ple tasks stay light while complex work gets stricter checks."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Skill | Focus |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| `hello-ui` | UI planning, design contracts, implementation mapping, visual validation |\n| `hello-a"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"pi` | API design, validation, error format, compatibility |\n| `hello-security` | auth, secrets, perm"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"issions, injection risks |\n| `hello-test` | TDD, coverage, edge cases, test structure |\n| `qa-review"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"` | unified quality review, verification commands, blocking fixes, delivery evidence, closeout |\n| `"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"helloagents` | command routing, workflow stage rules, project knowledge, and state coordination |\n| "},{"id":"p19s6","text":"`hello-errors` | error handling, logs, retry and recovery behavior |\n| `hello-perf` | performance, c"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"aching, query and rendering risks |\n| `hello-data` | database, migrations, transactions, indexes |\n|"},{"id":"p19s8","text":" `hello-arch` | architecture, boundaries, code size, maintainability |\n| `hello-debug` | bug diagnos"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"is and escalation when stuck |\n| `hello-subagent` | subagent delegation and result integration |\n| `"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"hello-write` | documentation, reports, and written deliverables |\n| `hello-reflect` | reusable lesso"},{"id":"p19s11","text":"ns and knowledge updates |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"All UI work first follows the shared UI quality baseline.\nIn host global mode, in initialized projec"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ts, or in explicit UI workflows, `hello-ui` adds deeper design-contract execution, design-system map"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ping, and visual validation on top of that baseline.\nWhen visual evidence is required, HelloAGENTS r"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"ecords it in the current session `artifacts/visual.json`."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### 2) Commands for different work styles"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Commands run inside the AI CLI chat with a `~` prefix. The command skill is read directly; unrelated"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" skills are not loaded unless the workflow needs them."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Command | Purpose |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| `~ask` | Interactive clarification: Q&A; to pin down goals, direction, scope, and constraints; doe"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"s not write files |\n| `~auto` | Chooses the main path and keeps going until delivery or a real block"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"er |\n| `~plan` | Requirements, solution design, task breakdown, and plan package |\n| `~build` | Impl"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ementation from the current request or an existing plan |\n| `~prd` | Modern product requirements doc"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"ument through guided dimension-by-dimension exploration |\n| `~loop` | Long-running entry; in Codex i"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"t prefers `/goal -> ~auto -> ~qa` |\n| `~init` | Initialize the project workflow and sync project kno"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"wledge |\n| `~test` | Write tests for a target module or recent change |\n| `~qa` | Run the unified qu"},{"id":"p24s8","text":"ality loop: review, verification commands, fixes, and closeout |\n| `~commit` | Generate a convention"},{"id":"p24s9","text":"al commit message and sync knowledge |\n| `~clean` | Archive finished plans and clean temporary runti"},{"id":"p24s10","text":"me files |\n| `~help` | Show commands and current settings |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Compatibility aliases:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- `~do` → `~build`\n- `~design` → `~plan`\n- `~review` → `~qa`\n- `~idea` → `~ask` (deprecated)"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Use `~ask` for clarifying requirements, comparing approaches, weighing value, and scoping — pure con"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"versation, no files created."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### 3) Project knowledge base"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"HelloAGENTS can create and maintain a project knowledge base under `.helloagents/`."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The knowledge base helps future turns understand the repo without re-discovering the same facts. It "},{"id":"p30s2","text":"dge base helps future turns understand the repo without re-discovering the same facts. It can store:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| File or directory | Purpose |"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| `context.md` | project overview, stack, architecture, module index |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"### What is the role of `docs/`?"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"`docs/` is reference material for users and AI agents. It may lag behind implementation; runtime beh"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"avior is defined by source code, rule templates, skills, templates, and tests."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"### What is the difference between standby and global?"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"`standby` is lighter and explicit. It deploys rules to selected CLIs while leaving each repo uniniti"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"alized until you run `~init`."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"`global` applies full rules broadly at the host level. Claude, Gemini, and Grok use native plugin, e"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"xtension, or marketplace installs. Cursor and Codex use native local-plugin paths; Cursor specifical"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"ly materializes a real plugin copy under `~/.cursor/plugins/local/helloagents`.\nIf you mainly want C"},{"id":"p37s4","text":"odex app/plugin discoverability, use `global`. If you mainly want a lighter, explicit project workfl"},{"id":"p37s5","text":"coverability, use `global`. If you mainly want a lighter, explicit project workflow, keep `standby`."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
